[ti:Still I Rise]
[00:07.48][Intro]
[00:07.56]Midnight hums in shades of blue
[00:13.40]A map unwritten, waiting to be drawn anew
[00:37.68][Verse]
[00:37.76]I walk where the streetlight loses its name
[00:42.36]Learning the language of a different rain
[00:47.24]Each wrong turn leaves a mark on my sleeve
[00:52.60]Proof of the roads I was scared to believe
[00:56.76]The horizon moves, so I move with it too
[00:59.52]Past all the rules that never came true
[01:01.80]I wear the unknown like a second skin
[01:04.40]Keeping one small match alive in the wind
[01:07.48]Still I rise before the fade
[01:12.40]Still I chase the light I made
[01:16.64]Out on the edge where tomorrow waits
[01:21.56]I'm becoming what tomorrow makes
[01:46.00][Verse]
[01:46.08]Deep in the fog, I found a steadier hand
[01:48.76]Every river redrew where I stand
[01:50.76]I keep small hours like coins in my coat
[01:53.36]Warm from the crossing, enough to stay afloat
[01:55.64]They watched from the shore while I learned to swim
[01:58.12]Now even the tide has changed its hymn
[02:00.72]Softer than thunder, clear as the glass
[02:03.00]I build what will stay when the old days pass
[02:06.28]Still I rise before the fade
[02:11.20]Still I chase the light I made
[02:15.44]Out on the edge where tomorrow waits
[02:20.32]I'm becoming what tomorrow makes
[02:48.40][Bridge]
[02:48.48]I thought the map had to tell me where
[02:53.08]But dawn found my footprints already there
[02:57.64]No finish line, no hand to hold
[03:00.08]Just my own fire against the cold
[03:24.52][Chorus]
[03:24.60]Still I rise before the fade
[03:29.44]Still I chase the light I made
[03:33.76]Out on the edge where tomorrow waits
[03:38.64]I'm becoming what tomorrow makes
